# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

Removing this resource from Terraform management leaves the GitHub setting in place.
{{- if .HasImportIDConfig }}

## Import the current setting
{{- if or (eq .Name "githubsettings_repository_archived_settings") (eq .Name "githubsettings_repository_secret_scanning_validity_checks") (eq .Name "githubsettings_organization_recorded_settings") }}

Read the current values with the GitHub CLI. Set [`GITHUB_TOKEN`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/elephant-evergreen/githubsettings/latest/docs#authentication) first so this command and Terraform use the same token. Replace `OWNER`{{ if ne .Name "githubsettings_organization_recorded_settings" }} and `REPOSITORY`{{ end }}.

{{ codefile "shell" (printf "examples/resources/%s/read-current.sh" .Name) }}

{{ if eq .Name "githubsettings_repository_secret_scanning_validity_checks" -}}
Use the reported `enabled` or `disabled` as `status`. If the result is empty or `null`, check the repository's security settings and confirm that the account can see the [security settings in the repository API response](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/repos/repos#get-a-repository). An absent value does not indicate `disabled`.
{{- else if eq .Name "githubsettings_repository_archived_settings" -}}
Confirm that `archived` is `true`. Use the other returned values as resource arguments. If a merge setting is missing, check the repository access and the [API requirements for merge settings](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/repos/repos#get-a-repository).
{{- else -}}
Use the returned values as resource arguments. If an expected field is `null`, check the token's organization Administration access and the [response for your organization](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/orgs/orgs#get-an-organization).
{{- end }}
{{- end }}

Add the import block below to a Terraform project configured with `elephant-evergreen/githubsettings`. The [quickstart](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/elephant-evergreen/githubsettings/latest/docs#import-a-policy) shows the provider block and initialization. Replace the example ID and address with those of your resource.

{{ tffile .ImportIDConfigFile }}

1. Add the resource block with arguments that match the current GitHub values.
2. Run `terraform plan -out=adopt.tfplan`. For one import, expect `1 to import, 0 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy`. If the plan proposes a change, compare the differing values with the current policy and save a new plan.
3. Run `terraform apply adopt.tfplan` once the saved plan contains only the import. The next `terraform plan` should report `No changes`.
{{- end }}
